senses
  entry
    definition "the shape or manner in which things come together and a connection is made"
    id oewn-13934166-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms (articulation joint juncture junction)
  entry
    definition "a set containing all and only the members of two or more given sets"
    examples ("let C be the union of the sets A and B")
    id oewn-08015154-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms (union sum)
  entry
    definition "become part of; become a member of a group or organization"
    examples ("He joined the Communist Party as a young man")
    id oewn-02439823-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms ("fall in" "get together")
  entry
    definition "cause to become joined or linked"
    examples ("join these two parts so that they fit together")
    id oewn-01297878-v
    partOfSpeech v
  entry
    definition "come into the company of"
    examples ("She joined him for a drink")
    id oewn-02604762-v
    partOfSpeech v
  entry
    definition "make contact or come together"
    examples ("The two roads join here")
    id oewn-01293672-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (conjoin)
  entry
    definition "be or become joined or united or linked"
    examples ("The two streets connect to become a highway" "Our paths joined" "The travelers linked up again at the airport")
    id oewn-02628315-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (connect link "link up" unite)
